.TH EUCLID-CLI-EKM-LIST-KEYS 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ekm-list-keys \- list existing encryption keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ekm list-keys
[\fB\-\-page\-size\fR|\fB\-s\fR \fICOUNT\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-index\fR|\fB\-i\fR \fIINDEX\fR]
[\fB\-\-sort\-column\fR|\fB\-c\fR \fICOLUMN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists all keys. Paginated:
.B \-\-page\-size
defaults to \fI10\fR,
.B \-\-page\-index
to \fI0\fR,
.B \-\-sort\-column
to \fIname\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-page\-size " " \fICOUNT\fR
Number of keys to return per page. Defaults to \fI10\fR.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-page\-index " " \fIINDEX\fR
Zero-based page index to return. Defaults to \fI0\fR.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-sort\-column " " \fICOLUMN\fR
Column to sort by. Defaults to \fIname\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The listing was retrieved and printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or the
server rejected the request.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ekm list-keys

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ekm list-keys \e
    --page-size 25 --page-index 1 --sort-column algorithm
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ekm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-create-key (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-encrypt (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-decrypt (1)
